WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:02.640
Have you ever wondered

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:06.560
if there are more natural ways
to lower your high blood pressure,

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:09.520
guard against Alzheimer's,
lose weight, and feel better?

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:12.720
Well, it turns out there is!

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:15.200
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:18.640
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:22.000
Today, the effects of
dairy milk on our health.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:25.120
And we start with the
so-called “milk pus test”

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:27.200
(that's actually what it's called)

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:31.440
and what it tells us
about the U.S. milk supply.

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:34.320
Dairy cows might normally live
for about 20 years,

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:36.240
but they are typically
slaughtered for hamburger

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:37.920
after they're just
a few years old,

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:41.440
when they produce less milk
and their profitability drops.

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:45.680
But another leading cause
of cow culling is mastitis,

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:47.280
udder inflammation
and infections,

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:51.360
which affects 99.7 percent
of all dairy operations

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:53.200
in the United States.

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:56.800
Because of the mastitis epidemic
in the U.S. dairy herd,

00:00:56.800 --> 00:01:00.240
the dairy industry continues
to demand that American milk

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:02.480
retain among
the highest allowable

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:04.480
"somatic cell" concentration,

00:01:04.480 --> 00:01:06.800
nearly twice as much
as the rest of the world--

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:10.160
750,000 cells per milliliter.

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:12.800
The concentration
in milk from healthy udders

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:15.440
should be less than 100,000.

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:18.320
These somatic cells are mostly
white blood cells,

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:20.880
so, when you get up
to around 200,000,

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:22.400
which is, like,
a million per teaspoon,

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:24.960
the udder is likely
to be infected.

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:28.240
So, the somatic cell counts
in the bulk milk tanks

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:30.560
reflect the level of infection.

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:32.240
Basically,
if the bulk milk tank,

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:34.240
which can hold
thousands of gallons,

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:38.400
averages 200,000, then 15
percent of the contributing cows

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:39.440
are likely infected.

00:01:39.440 --> 00:01:41.360
At a concentration of 400,000,

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:43.680
which is more in line
with international standards,

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:46.480
a third of the cows
are likely infected.

00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:50.800
And staying within the 750,000
U.S. limit for Grade A milk

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:53.520
could reflect that
about two thirds of the cows

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:54.880
are infected.

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:59.360
Now, somatic cells are not
synonymous with pus cells,

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:02.640
as has sometimes been
misleadingly suggested.

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:05.040
Just as normal human blood
and breast milk

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:07.360
contain low levels
of white blood cells,

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:09.080
so does milk from healthy cows.

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:12.560
That's something we've known
for more than a century.

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:16.160
The problem is that many
of our cows are not healthy.

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:18.960
According to the latest
national government survey,

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:21.120
about one in four dairy cows
in the United States

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:23.200
suffers from clinical mastitis,

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:26.400
the second leading cause
of death on dairy farms.

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:30.000
This is why the average somatic
cell concentration of U.S. milk

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.240
is that
of a likely infected udder,

00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:35.040
at 204,000 cells per milliliter.

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:38.960
How much actual pus
does that translate to?

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:42.000
Although the industry doesn't
like to talk about pus cells,

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:43.200
the fact that pus is present

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:46.560
in milk from inflamed
mammary glands is a given.

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:49.280
But what constitutes
pus in milk?

00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:52.560
The quote-unquote
"milk pus test" was introduced

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:53.760
more than a century ago.

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:55.520
It pooled milk
from infected cows

00:02:55.520 --> 00:02:59.840
that was estimated to contain
up to 2.5 percent pus by volume.

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:04.080
And we'd really like to see
no more than, like, 0.1 percent.

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:06.880
So, what does 204,000
cells per milliliter,

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:11.040
the national U.S. average,
translate to?

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:13.600
That's a million cells
per teaspoon of milk.

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:15.920
A million cells per spoonful
sounds like a lot,

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:17.920
but pus is really concentrated.

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:20.080
So, how much pus is there
in a glass of milk?

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:21.200
Not much.

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:22.480
If you take the national average

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:24.560
and subtract the number
of white blood cells

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:26.000
you might see in normal milk,

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:29.040
you get about 100,000
inflammatory white blood cells

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:29.920
per milliliter,

00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:32.400
or about 25 million per cup.

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:35.440
Then it just depends on the
cellular concentration of pus.

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:37.440
Although straight pus may have

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:39.840
80,000 cells per microliter
or less,

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:40.800
to be conservative,

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:42.880
the most concentrated
I could find for straight pus

00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:45.040
was about 150,000.

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:48.400
Note that's per microliter,
not per milliliter.

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:50.640
So, if there are about
25 million cells per cup,

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:54.000
and a microliter of pus
contains about 150,000 cells,

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:55.040
that would come out to be

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:58.160
about 150 microliters of pus
per glass of milk.

00:03:58.160 --> 00:04:00.960
There are about
50 microliters in a drop,

00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:04.880
so there'd only be a few drops
of pus per glass on average.

00:04:04.880 --> 00:04:07.360
And you can apparently taste
the difference.

00:04:07.360 --> 00:04:09.840
One of the major problems
associated with mastitis

00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:12.400
is the flavor and texture
defects.

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:15.280
Milk with high somatic
cell counts looks the same,

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:18.320
but evidently doesn't smell
or taste as good.

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:20.640
The large amounts of pus
in mastitic milk

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:23.360
may be aesthetically
objectionable,

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:26.320
but it's important to note
this is not a food safety issue,

00:04:26.320 --> 00:04:28.160
thanks to pasteurization.

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:29.920
The dairy industry emphasizes

00:04:29.920 --> 00:04:32.800
that ingesting large amounts
of bovine white blood cells

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:35.040
has not been shown
to be harmful.

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:37.760
No matter how inflamed
and infected udders get,

00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:39.520
the pus gets cooked.

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:42.560
But just as parents may not
want to feed their children

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:43.680
fecal bacteria in meat,

00:04:43.680 --> 00:04:45.920
even if it's
irradiated fecal bacteria,

00:04:45.920 --> 00:04:48.080
as the director of the
Food Policy Institute put it:

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:51.120
"Irradiated poop won't make you
sick, but it's still poop,"

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:53.760
parents may not want
to have their children sip

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:56.880
pasteurized pus.

00:04:56.880 --> 00:04:57.760
In our next story,

00:04:57.760 --> 00:05:02.000
we look at the role milk may
play in triggering Parkinson’s disease.

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:05.600
Parkinson's disease is a
neurodegenerative brain disorder

00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:09.840
that affects millions of people.
What causes it?

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:13.520
Well, if you look at lifestyle factors
associated with Parkinson's disease,

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:15.840
the strongest dietary association

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:19.920
with increased risk of Parkinson's
disease is dairy consumption.

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:22.960
In fact, dairy products are the
only food group that has been

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:26.240
consistently associated with a
high risk of developing Parkinson's.

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:32.080
Five large prospective studies have
confirmed the link — including the two

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:34.480
Harvard cohorts, the Harvard
Nurses' Health Study and

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:35.520
other Health Professionals —

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:39.200
which followed more than a hundred
thousand people for decades,

00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:42.560
in the largest analysis of dairy
and Parkinson's disease to date,

00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:46.240
analyzing more than a thousand
newly diagnosed cases.

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:50.880
And all the studies found a link
between dairy and Parkinson's,

00:05:50.880 --> 00:05:55.440
most finding a significant link:
about a 50% increased risk overall

00:05:55.440 --> 00:05:58.640
in those drinking the most milk,
compared to those drinking the least

00:05:58.640 --> 00:06:05.360
at a p value of less than 0.00001,
meaning less than 1 in 100,000

00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:09.120
you'd only get a finding
that extreme by chance.

00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:14.320
Okay, but why is there a link at all?
Despite clear-cut associations

00:06:14.320 --> 00:06:17.360
between milk intake and
Parkinson's disease incidence,

00:06:17.360 --> 00:06:21.200
there is no rational explanation,
concluded one review.

00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:26.160
A year later though, we got a clue:
"Midlife milk consumption

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:29.920
and substantia nigra neuron
density at death."

00:06:29.920 --> 00:06:34.320
What does that mean? Parkinson's is
caused when most of the nerve cells

00:06:34.320 --> 00:06:37.040
in a critical part of
the brain are killed off.

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:39.600
So if you go back and see how
much milk people were drinking

00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:43.680
in their 40s, 50s, and 60s, and then
look at their brains on autopsy

00:06:43.680 --> 00:06:47.040
and count how many of these
critical neurons they had left,

00:06:47.040 --> 00:06:50.960
in every single quadrant
neuron density was maximized

00:06:50.960 --> 00:06:52.960
in those who
consumed no milk

00:06:52.960 --> 00:06:56.160
and lowest in those who
consumed the most milk.

00:06:56.160 --> 00:06:59.680
Even after removing the Parkinson's
cases, those drinking two cups of milk

00:06:59.680 --> 00:07:04.480
a day had up to 40% fewer nerve
cells in that critical brain region.

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:07.680
What's in milk that could
be wiping out brain cells?

00:07:07.680 --> 00:07:10.560
Among those who drank
the most milk, residues

00:07:10.560 --> 00:07:15.760
of the pesticide heptachlor epoxide
were found in 9 out of 10 brains.

00:07:15.760 --> 00:07:20.160
A-ha, so maybe the finding of pesticide
residues more commonly in the brains

00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:23.680
of those who drank the most milk
could explain how milk could be

00:07:23.680 --> 00:07:27.600
cause-and-effect related
to Parkinson's disease risk.

00:07:27.600 --> 00:07:30.720
Now that's not the only
potential explanation.

00:07:30.720 --> 00:07:33.440
Remember my video on how
meat contains that clumpy

00:07:33.440 --> 00:07:37.840
neurotoxic protein alpha-synuclein?
Well, dairy products may contain

00:07:37.840 --> 00:07:41.760
trace amounts as well, but we
don't have confirmation of that.

00:07:41.760 --> 00:07:45.520
Could the milk sugar galactose
be the missing link?

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:49.680
That's what lactose in milk breaks
down into in the body, and galactose

00:07:49.680 --> 00:07:54.800
is what's used to induce aging, to
experimentally cause aging in the brain.

00:07:54.800 --> 00:07:58.080
When you drink it, the galactose
is picked up by your brain

00:07:58.080 --> 00:08:01.440
within a few hours, and
for doses above 100 mg/kg,

00:08:02.480 --> 00:08:05.280
it appears that galactose
can cause pathological

00:08:05.280 --> 00:08:09.760
alterations in brain cells, similar to
those observed in Parkinson's disease.

00:08:09.760 --> 00:08:12.960
And these quantities can be
reached and surpassed

00:08:12.960 --> 00:08:17.360
with the simple daily consumption
of two glasses of milk,

00:08:17.360 --> 00:08:20.800
the main dietary source
of galactose in humans.

00:08:20.800 --> 00:08:23.680
And of all your brain cells,
those dopaminergic neurons,

00:08:23.680 --> 00:08:26.320
the ones that you need
to retain to prevent Parkinson's,

00:08:26.320 --> 00:08:29.440
may be more vulnerable
to galactose-induced damage,

00:08:29.440 --> 00:08:33.760
galactose-induced oxidative stress.
Galactose may also explain

00:08:33.760 --> 00:08:37.440
the findings that link milk drinking
with higher death rates.

00:08:37.440 --> 00:08:40.960
Now you may be thinking, well,
duh, the saturated butterfat

00:08:40.960 --> 00:08:44.720
is just cutting people's life short,
but higher mortality with higher milk

00:08:44.720 --> 00:08:48.560
consumption is observed,
irrespective of the milk fat content.

00:08:48.560 --> 00:08:53.120
Skim milk might be fat free,
but it's not lactose free.

00:08:53.120 --> 00:08:55.680
Can't you just use
lactose-free milk?

00:08:55.680 --> 00:09:00.160
What about Lactaid? That
has the lactase enzyme added

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:04.800
to make lactose-free milk, but it just
breaks down the lactose into galactose

00:09:04.800 --> 00:09:07.200
in the carton rather
than in your gut,

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:10.400
so you're still ingesting the
same amount of galactose.

00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:13.200
Perhaps no wonder then that
greater milk intake at midlife

00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:16.560
may be associated with
greater rate of cognitive decline.

00:09:17.120 --> 00:09:21.680
I mean, researchers use galactose
to create brain aging in the laboratory.

00:09:21.680 --> 00:09:25.120
Administration of D-galactose,
a metabolic derivative of lactose,

00:09:25.120 --> 00:09:28.320
has been extensively used
to mimic cognitive aging

00:09:28.320 --> 00:09:31.040
through oxidative stress
in animal models.

00:09:31.040 --> 00:09:34.080
Compared to those who said
they "almost never" drink milk,

00:09:34.080 --> 00:09:36.640
those drinking more than a glass
a day appear more likely

00:09:36.640 --> 00:09:40.800
to suffer a global decline
in their cognitive function.

00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:42.160
Finally today,

00:09:42.160 --> 00:09:46.880
how to reduce the risk of premature
death from dairy consumption.

00:09:46.880 --> 00:09:49.360
In my video
on milk and bones,

00:09:49.360 --> 00:09:51.520
I discussed
this set of studies,

00:09:51.520 --> 00:09:54.640
following a hundred thousand
people for up to two decades,

00:09:54.640 --> 00:09:57.760
finding a 60% higher risk
of hip fracture

00:09:57.760 --> 00:09:59.920
among women who drank
a lot of milk.

00:09:59.920 --> 00:10:03.600
The researchers suggested it
might be due to the galactose,

00:10:03.600 --> 00:10:06.960
which is a breakdown product
of the milk sugar lactose,

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:09.680
based on the fact that people
with high levels in their blood,

00:10:09.680 --> 00:10:12.960
because they were born with an
inability to detoxify the stuff,

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:15.280
can end up
with weakened bones.

00:10:15.280 --> 00:10:18.640
But that's not all
galactose can do.

00:10:18.640 --> 00:10:21.360
Galactose is what scientists use

00:10:21.360 --> 00:10:24.880
to cause accelerated aging
in lab animals,

00:10:24.880 --> 00:10:27.680
since it's so successful
at mimicking aging

00:10:27.680 --> 00:10:30.720
by inducing degenerative changes
in the brain,

00:10:30.720 --> 00:10:33.360
heart, lungs, liver,
kidney, etc.

00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:36.480
"Life-shortened animals
showed neurodegeneration,

00:10:36.480 --> 00:10:39.120
mental retardation,
and cognitive dysfunction,

00:10:39.120 --> 00:10:40.640
diminished immune responses

00:10:40.640 --> 00:10:43.520
and a reduction
of reproductive ability."

00:10:43.520 --> 00:10:45.120
And it doesn't take much,

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:46.400
just the human equivalent

00:10:46.400 --> 00:10:49.760
of one to two glasses worth
of milk a day.

00:10:49.760 --> 00:10:52.960
However, humans aren't rodents.

00:10:52.960 --> 00:10:55.200
For example, we've known
for nearly a century

00:10:55.200 --> 00:10:57.680
that you can cause cataracts
in rats

00:10:57.680 --> 00:11:00.960
by feeding them lots
of lactose or galactose,

00:11:00.960 --> 00:11:03.520
but the epidemiological data
is mixed

00:11:03.520 --> 00:11:06.640
as to whether dairy
is doing the same in people.

00:11:06.640 --> 00:11:09.360
The Swedish studies didn't
just look at bone, though,

00:11:09.360 --> 00:11:11.840
but milk and mortality.

00:11:11.840 --> 00:11:15.760
More milk was associated
with more death.

00:11:15.760 --> 00:11:17.760
In women,
three glasses of milk a day

00:11:17.760 --> 00:11:21.520
was associated with nearly twice
the risk of dying prematurely.

00:11:21.520 --> 00:11:23.120
The medical journal editorial

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:25.920
accompanying the study
emphasized that,

00:11:25.920 --> 00:11:27.440
given the rise
in milk consumption

00:11:27.440 --> 00:11:28.640
around the world,

00:11:28.640 --> 00:11:30.720
the "role of milk in mortality

00:11:30.720 --> 00:11:34.560
needs to be established
definitively now."

00:11:34.560 --> 00:11:37.920
With the then-largest-ever study
on milk intake and mortality

00:11:37.920 --> 00:11:40.320
suggesting such adverse effects,

00:11:40.320 --> 00:11:43.600
Harvard researchers stepped in
with three of their cohorts

00:11:43.600 --> 00:11:45.920
to form a study twice as big

00:11:45.920 --> 00:11:49.040
to see if the earlier findings
were just a fluke.

00:11:49.040 --> 00:11:51.440
Following more than
200,000 men and women

00:11:51.440 --> 00:11:53.280
for up to three decades,

00:11:53.280 --> 00:11:55.920
they confirmed the bad news.

00:11:55.920 --> 00:11:57.920
Those who consumed more dairy

00:11:57.920 --> 00:11:59.600
lived significantly shorter
lives.

00:11:59.600 --> 00:12:02.880
Every half serving more
of regular milk a day

00:12:02.880 --> 00:12:06.320
was associated with
9% increased risk of dying

00:12:06.320 --> 00:12:08.000
from cardiovascular disease,

00:12:08.000 --> 00:12:10.400
11% increased risk
of dying from cancer,

00:12:10.400 --> 00:12:12.240
and an 11% increased risk
of dying

00:12:12.240 --> 00:12:14.960
from all causes put together.

00:12:14.960 --> 00:12:16.560
This is all the more remarkable

00:12:16.560 --> 00:12:18.880
since milk drinking
is typically associated

00:12:18.880 --> 00:12:20.080
with healthier habits,

00:12:20.080 --> 00:12:23.280
like more exercise
and less smoking and drinking,

00:12:23.280 --> 00:12:26.240
though they did try to control
for all these factors.

00:12:26.240 --> 00:12:29.840
Of course it does matter
what you eat instead.

00:12:29.840 --> 00:12:31.280
This Harvard analysis published

00:12:31.280 --> 00:12:32.880
in the New England Journal
of Medicine,

00:12:32.880 --> 00:12:34.880
found that swapping dairy
for meat,

00:12:34.880 --> 00:12:37.360
red meat, poultry, or fish,

00:12:37.360 --> 00:12:41.280
would not be expected
to do your body any favors,

00:12:41.280 --> 00:12:44.400
and you would be expected
to live longer eating dairy

00:12:44.400 --> 00:12:47.280
than eggs or processed meat.

00:12:47.280 --> 00:12:48.560
It's only when you swap dairy

00:12:48.560 --> 00:12:50.720
for plant-based sources
of protein

00:12:50.720 --> 00:12:54.800
did they find a significant drop
in mortality risk.

00:12:54.800 --> 00:12:56.720
When all of the milk
and mortality studies

00:12:56.720 --> 00:12:57.840
are put together,

00:12:57.840 --> 00:12:59.600
it appears
the excess mortality risk

00:12:59.600 --> 00:13:03.760
is limited to regular as opposed
to low-fat, like skim milk.

00:13:03.760 --> 00:13:07.760
This suggests it may be more
of a saturated fat issue,

00:13:07.760 --> 00:13:11.280
though that doesn't explain why
soured, or fermented milk

00:13:11.280 --> 00:13:12.960
appears to have
the opposite impact.

00:13:12.960 --> 00:13:16.560
So maybe it's both the butterfat
and the galactose.

00:13:16.560 --> 00:13:19.360
A randomized crossover study
of low-fat dairy,

00:13:19.360 --> 00:13:21.920
fermented dairy,
and unfermented dairy

00:13:21.920 --> 00:13:23.200
found that study subjects

00:13:23.200 --> 00:13:26.240
had significantly higher
IL-6 inflammation levels

00:13:26.240 --> 00:13:28.960
during unfermented
regular dairy weeks

00:13:28.960 --> 00:13:30.720
compared to when they were
switched to either

00:13:30.720 --> 00:13:34.160
the fermented
or low-fat dairy products.

00:13:34.160 --> 00:13:38.240
The fermentation process can
eliminate some of the galactose.

00:13:38.240 --> 00:13:41.760
As we age, our ability
to detoxify galactose

00:13:41.760 --> 00:13:44.560
declines by as much as 40%,

00:13:44.560 --> 00:13:46.240
which would make it
even more important

00:13:46.240 --> 00:13:48.240
to avoid dairy later in life

00:13:48.240 --> 00:13:51.440
if indeed galactose
is the culprit.

00:13:51.440 --> 00:13:53.680
But if galactose
does its dirty work

00:13:53.680 --> 00:13:55.920
through oxidation
and inflammation,

00:13:55.920 --> 00:13:58.240
might increased fruit
and vegetable intake

00:13:58.240 --> 00:14:00.480
help mediate some of the harm?

00:14:00.480 --> 00:14:03.360
In animals,
galactose-induced aging

00:14:03.360 --> 00:14:06.080
can be slowed by fruit
and vegetable consumption.

00:14:06.080 --> 00:14:08.720
For example,
feeding rats blueberries

00:14:08.720 --> 00:14:13.440
can decrease the brain damage
induced by the milk sugar.

00:14:13.440 --> 00:14:14.480
Might it be able to help

00:14:14.480 --> 00:14:16.400
with the higher levels
of oxidative stress

00:14:16.400 --> 00:14:19.600
and inflammation found
among human milk drinkers?

00:14:19.600 --> 00:14:22.560
Unfortunately, women drinking
three or more glasses of milk

00:14:22.560 --> 00:14:24.800
a day had more than twice
the risk of hip fractures

00:14:24.800 --> 00:14:27.360
compared to women drinking
less than a glass a day

00:14:27.360 --> 00:14:31.360
regardless of whether
they were eating more, or less,

00:14:31.360 --> 00:14:32.800
fruits and vegetables.

00:14:32.800 --> 00:14:36.800
But, those high milk consumers

00:14:36.800 --> 00:14:39.440
consuming five or more servings
of fruits and vegetables a day

00:14:39.440 --> 00:14:42.480
did reduce their chance
of dying prematurely

00:14:42.480 --> 00:14:45.920
to just 60% greater
than those drinking less milk,

00:14:45.920 --> 00:14:47.600
so antioxidant rich foods

00:14:47.600 --> 00:14:50.400
may be able to modify
the elevated death rate

00:14:50.400 --> 00:14:53.520
associated with
high milk consumption.

00:14:53.520 --> 00:14:56.640
Highly influential
advocacy organizations,

00:14:56.640 --> 00:14:59.200
such as the US National
Osteoporosis Foundation

00:14:59.200 --> 00:15:00.560
or the Europe-based

00:15:00.560 --> 00:15:02.880
International
Osteoporosis Foundation,

00:15:02.880 --> 00:15:06.640
continue to push dairy, drugs,
and calcium supplements,

00:15:06.640 --> 00:15:11.040
despite the countervailing
evidence that I've reviewed.

00:15:11.040 --> 00:15:14.480
Why do they keep pushing dairy,
drugs, and supplements?

00:15:14.480 --> 00:15:17.280
Perhaps because their
objectivity is compromised

00:15:17.280 --> 00:15:19.840
by the influence
of their commercial sponsors

00:15:19.840 --> 00:15:23.120
that include companies
that market, you guessed it,

00:15:23.120 --> 00:15:25.600
dairy, drugs,
and supplements.

00:15:25.600 --> 00:15:28.160
Most recent reviews
on dairy and osteoporosis

00:15:28.160 --> 00:15:29.920
in the English-language
medical literature

00:15:29.920 --> 00:15:30.800
were found to be written

00:15:30.800 --> 00:15:34.240
by those with ties
to the dairy industry.

00:15:34.240 --> 00:15:37.120
The primary justification
for inclusion of dairy

00:15:37.120 --> 00:15:38.960
in federal nutrition
recommendations

00:15:38.960 --> 00:15:41.600
is based on
purported bone benefits

00:15:41.600 --> 00:15:45.200
that are not supported
by the available evidence.

00:15:45.200 --> 00:15:47.920
What if dietary guidelines
were fashioned

00:15:47.920 --> 00:15:50.240
without commercial influence?

00:15:50.240 --> 00:15:55.360
In 2019, Canada decided
to exclude industry reports

00:15:55.360 --> 00:15:56.720
and stick to the science

00:15:56.720 --> 00:15:58.880
in the formation
of their new dietary guidelines.

00:15:58.880 --> 00:16:00.320
What a concept.

00:16:00.320 --> 00:16:02.880
Major changes
include the new emphasis

00:16:02.880 --> 00:16:05.520
on plant-based food intake,
limiting junk,

00:16:05.520 --> 00:16:10.480
and...the removal
of the dairy food group.

